    <SectionHeading eyebrow="In practice">Where to put text, captions and your logo</SectionHeading>
    <ul class="tips">
      <li><strong>Hook text:</strong> just below the top third of the screen, roughly y 300–700 px. The top ~220–290 px sit under the tabs and search bar.</li>
      <li><strong>Captions / subtitles:</strong> the default “very bottom” position lands under the post caption. Move captions to the middle or ~700 px up from the bottom (y ≈ 1100–1250); the combined safe zone is the safest bet if you cross-post.</li>
      <li><strong>Logo:</strong> small and simple, near the top edge of the safe zone rather than in a corner. The bottom-right corner is under the buttons or the sound disc on almost every platform.</li>
      <li><strong>Faces and products:</strong> centred, slightly in from the right edge. The background can run edge to edge; only what must be read needs to be inside the safe zone.</li>
      <li><strong>Reels comment replies:</strong> the comment sticker stays on screen for the whole video and can cover the upper middle. Plan the hook and face below it, or drag the sticker to an empty spot before posting.</li>
      <li><strong>Running it as an ad:</strong> organic margins aren't enough. For Meta ads, keep the bottom 35% (≈670 px) clear; that's where the call-to-action button appears.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
